    "narrative": "Today\u2019s primary objective is to exploit the favorable conditions facing our high-upside speed threats. **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (69.26) anchor the lineup, offering the highest efficiency scores of the day. **Dylan Beavers** benefits significantly from the combination of a favorable park and a +10% order premium, while **Geraldo Perdomo**\u2019s matchup against Mikolas provides a strong SP skill advantage (+17%), positioning both to provide the elite stolen base production we prioritize. **Bryce Harper** (68.70) remains an essential start, bolstered by his #3 spot in the order and positive park factors, which help him maintain a strong floor despite facing a decent arm in Warren.\n\nWe have strategically opted to bench **Daulton Varsho** (43.90), who was our most difficult cut today. While **Daulton Varsho** benefits from a slight boost for potential stolen bases against a slow-delivering pitcher, his efficiency was capped by a negative wind factor and a suboptimal platoon matchup against Suarez, ultimately placing him below our utility thresholds. Conversely, **Taylor Ward** (64.26) earns his spot in the outfield primarily due to a massive +16% park adjustment, which outweighs the marginal risk of his platoon split. We are cautiously monitoring **Cal Raleigh** (43.30); while he remains in the lineup, his production will be tested against the elite arm of deGrom, whose 3.07 xERA necessitates a tempered expectation for the catcher slot today. With most of our starters facing favorable pitchers (xERA > 4.00), we are well-positioned to maintain our efficiency targets.",
